# ANEL Manager

A modern Node.js library for controlling ANEL power outlets via UDP protocol.

## Features

- 🔄 Modern async/await API
- 🛡️ Global command queuing to protect devices
- 📡 Real-time status monitoring via UDP broadcasts
- ⚡ Fast lane option for emergency commands
- 🐳 Docker-friendly environment configuration
- 🔌 Zero external dependencies

## Installation

```bash
npm install anel-manager
```

## Quick Start

```javascript
const ANELManager = require('anel-manager');
const manager = new ANELManager();

// Turn on port 0
await manager.setPowerState('192.168.1.100', 0, 'on');

// Listen for status updates
manager.on('status', (data) => {
  console.log(`${data.ip} port ${data.port}: ${data.state} (${data.name})`);
});

// Query device status (triggers status broadcast)
await manager.getPowerState('192.168.1.100', 0);
```

## Configuration

Configure via environment variables:

```bash
ANEL_COMMAND_DELAY=0.5              # Seconds between commands
ANEL_UDP_SEND_PORT=9975             # Command send port
ANEL_UDP_RECEIVE_PORT=9977          # Status receive port
ANEL_DEFAULT_USER=root              # Default username
ANEL_DEFAULT_PASSWORD=brotwurst     # Default password
ANEL_CONNECTION_TIMEOUT=5000        # Connection timeout (ms)
```

## API Reference

### Power Control

```javascript
// Set power state
await manager.setPowerState(ip, port, state, options)
// ip: device IP address
// port: port number (0-based)  
// state: 'on' | 'off' | 1 | 0
// options: {user?, password?, fastLane?}

// Query power state (returns void, emits 'status' event)
await manager.getPowerState(ip, port, options)
```

### Fast Lane Commands

```javascript
// Emergency shutdown bypassing queue
await manager.setPowerState('192.168.1.100', 0, 'off', {fastLane: true});
```

### Events

```javascript
// Individual port status updates
manager.on('status', (data) => {
  console.log(data); // {ip, port, state, name}
});
```

## Usage Examples

### Basic Control

```javascript
const manager = new ANELManager();

// Turn on device port 0
await manager.setPowerState('192.168.1.100', 0, 'on');

// Custom credentials
await manager.setPowerState('192.168.1.100', 1, 'off', {
  user: 'admin',
  password: 'secret'
});
```

### Status Monitoring

```javascript
// Listen for all status updates
manager.on('status', (data) => {
  console.log(`Device ${data.ip} port ${data.port} is ${data.state}`);
});

// Query specific device (triggers status broadcast)
await manager.getPowerState('192.168.1.100', 0);
```

### Emergency Control

```javascript
// Fast lane for immediate execution
await manager.setPowerState('192.168.1.100', 0, 'off', {fastLane: true});
```

## Requirements

- Node.js 16+
- Network access to ANEL devices (UDP ports 9975/9977)
- ANEL NET-CONTROL or compatible devices

## License

GPL-3.0

